# Mini RAG Project

A simple Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) project that demonstrates how documents can be converted into embeddings, stored as vectors, and searched using semantic similarity.

## 📌 Project Overview

This project implements the core retrieval part of a RAG pipeline using an AI notes PDF.

The PDF is:
1. Loaded and converted into text
2. Split into smaller chunks
3. Converted into vector embeddings
4. Stored in ChromaDB
5. Queried using semantic similarity
6. Used to retrieve the most relevant text passages

## ✨ Features

- 📄 PDF document processing
- ✂️ Text chunking with overlapping sections
- 🧠 Sentence Transformer embeddings
- 🔎 Semantic similarity search
- 🗄️ ChromaDB vector database
- 📊 Top-3 relevant results retrieval
- 💻 Simple command-line interface

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- LangChain
- Sentence Transformers
- ChromaDB
- PyPDF
- NumPy

